# Task 1 – Problem Analysis & Objects

## 1. Inputs

- Vehicle registration number
- Vehicle type
- Entry time
- Parking facility details
- Pass details (if available)
## 2. Outputs

- Allocated parking slot
- Unique parking ticket
- Parking fee
- Updated parking availability
## 3. Main Objects

- Vehicle
- ParkingSlot
- ParkingFloor
- ParkingFacility
- ParkingTicket
- ParkingPass
- Payment
## 4. Object Responsibilities

| Object | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Vehicle | Stores vehicle details and type |
| ParkingSlot | Stores slot number and availability |
| ParkingFloor | Manages parking slots on a floor |
| ParkingFacility | Allocates and releases parking slots |
| ParkingTicket | Stores ticket, vehicle and entry details |
| ParkingPass | Identifies valid staff/student parking pass |
| Payment | Calculates and records parking fee |
## 5. Object Relationship

- A ParkingFacility contains multiple ParkingFloors.
- A ParkingFloor contains multiple ParkingSlots.
- A Vehicle is assigned to one ParkingSlot.
- A ParkingTicket is created for each parking entry.
- A ParkingPass is used by eligible staff or students.
- Payment is calculated when the vehicle exits.
